                <head>25. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On March 28, Frank Graham submitted his
                    report on the Kashmir dispute to the U.N. Security Council. The U.S. Mission
                    briefly summarized the report in telegram 1086 from New York, March 28: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Report follows pattern previously indicated to us by Graham. He states his hope two govts
                            will keep under consideration his proposal for high-level conference and
                            will find it possible promptly themselves make preparations for holding
                            such conference which would include on agenda basic differences they
                            find stand in way of settlement and such other matters they find would
                            contribute to progress toward implementation UNCIP resolutions and toward peaceful settlement.”
                            (Department of State, Central Files, 690D.91/3–2858)</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>For text of Graham’s report, see U.N. doc.
                    S/3984.</p>
            </div>
